# armour/man/scale_hang: the scale tassets on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6 / 27.4: the Imperial "scale with
# tassets"): two scaled plates hinged at the belt with a solid band hem, rigid (they shift whole in the flare, never bend).
# Finish regions: R the band hems, N the hinge courses, W a spot on the shadow tasset.
# Keys: the hang channel in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py (fill: scale).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
# (FORGE-LIMBS envelope r1) T5-T6 skirt flare (STYLE_P2 29.3): `armour.t5` views facing D/U, 1 px more past the hips on the lower half; flared copies of the replace views go before them. Generated by FORGE-LIMBS flare.py.
use person
body man
role armour scale
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
z 10

view D key rest origin 6 -1
|vzxyxwvywxwv
|vwwwwwvwwwwv
|vzyxxxvxxxxv
|vvvvvv.vvvvv
regions
